%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral'}}%%
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Client as Client (SDK or HTTP)
  participant Mw as apiKeyMiddleware
  participant Route as permissions.check handler
  participant Cache as permissionCache (60s TTL)
  participant DB as Postgres (via Prisma)

  Client->>Mw: GET /v1/permissions/check?userId, groupId, permission<br/>Authorization: Bearer jk_...
  Mw->>DB: ApiKey by prefix
  DB-->>Mw: gameId + hashedSecret
  Mw->>Mw: scrypt verify, check revokedAt
  Mw->>Route: c.var.gameId set, next()

  Route->>DB: Group WHERE id AND gameId AND softDeletedAt IS NULL
  DB-->>Route: group or null
  opt group missing or cross-game
    Route-->>Client: 404 not_found
  end

  Route->>Cache: get(gameId, groupId, userId, permission)
  alt cache hit (within 60s, not invalidated)
    Cache-->>Route: PermissionCheckResult
    Route-->>Client: 200 OK (cached)
  else cache miss
    Cache-->>Route: null
    Route->>DB: ExternalIdentity (gameId, externalUserId)
    DB-->>Route: junjoUserId or null
    alt no identity
      Route->>Cache: set { source: "none" }
      Route-->>Client: 200 { source: "none" }
    else identity resolved
      Route->>DB: GroupMember (groupId, junjoUserId)
      DB-->>Route: { status } or null
      alt no row, or status != active
        Route->>Cache: set { source: "none" }
        Route-->>Client: 200 { source: "none" }
      else active member
        Route->>DB: Game config (permissions.mode), once per request
        Route->>DB: MemberPermissionOverride (memberId, key IN candidate keys)
        DB-->>Route: matching overrides
        alt an override matches
          Route->>Cache: set { source: "override" }
          Route-->>Client: 200 { source: "override", allowed }
        else no override matches
          Route->>DB: roles reachable from MemberRole via RoleParent (recursive CTE)
          Route->>DB: RolePermission (reachable roles, key IN candidate keys)
          DB-->>Route: matching entries
          Route->>Route: nearest layer, then most specific key, then deny wins
          alt an entry decides
            Route->>Cache: set { source: "role", viaRoleId }
            Route-->>Client: 200 { source: "role", allowed }
          else nothing matches
            Route->>Cache: set { source: "default" }
            Route-->>Client: 200 { source: "default", allowed: false }
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end

  Note over Client,DB: Mutations (role assign/remove, role entry and parent writes, role delete,<br/>member override set/clear) call cache.invalidateGroup(groupId) after commit,<br/>and a permission mode switch clears the cache, so a stale answer flips within one round-trip.
